<title>UK: LIFFE sets early trading schedule after UK ballot.</title>
<headline>LIFFE sets early trading schedule after UK ballot.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-04-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>The London International Financial Futures and Options Exchange (LIFFE) said on Monday it would start trading in several contracts early on May 2, following the May 1 British election.</p>
<p>The exchange said pit trading will start as follows --</p>
<p>    Bund futures			     0600 GMT</p>
<p>    Bund futures options		   0602 GMT</p>
<p>    Gilt futures			     0615 GMT</p>
<p>    Gilt futures options		   0617 GMT</p>
<p>    Short sterling futures		 0620 GMT</p>
<p>    Short sterling futures options     0622 GMT</p>
<p>    FTSE 100 futures			 0625 GMT</p>
<p>    FTSE 100 futures options	     0625 GMT</p>
<p>&quot;The revised opening hours, for this day only will enable LIFFE members and their clients to react to the outcome of the general election earlier, in order to meet demand from Europe and the Far East,&quot; LIFFE said in a statement.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 6784</p>
</text>
